<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2966"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 9:54 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Also: It&#39;s right next to I135 &amp; near the where I135 crosses 400. Interesting but according to the always accurate ;&#40; Map Quest both 3rd &amp; Kansas streets dead end and you&#39;d have to loop around a couple of blocks to access the Freeway.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
