<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3700"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 3:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Q, my only fears rest in the fact that I almost always have a child with me while I am out doing these crazy things. I would glady get a pic of that address for you - and I will, if Catcher doesn&#39;t beat me to it. The ice is a bit of a factor for me right now. Maybe by Sunday?  <BR> <BR>Did you hear about the Eagle ad for the BTK documentary? It&#39;s in the Go section of today&#39;s paper. Some UNSUB films from CA wants interested parties to come to Evergreen park on Jan 14th for interviews. Do you know where Evergreen park is? 27th and Woodland. Mighty close to North Riverside. That gives me the willies. Why there? Gotta be a reason. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3700-->
<!--Post: 3706--><!--Time: 1105145816-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3706"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 4:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Maybe Tom is going a day or two early... <BR> <BR>BTW: Has the power outage and possible phone outs brought up any local talk about BTK being out and about more than normal? <BR> <BR>I&#39;m assuming you got your power back since your here. <BR> <BR>That park address for the movie is close as is Riverside to at least one crime scene and they&#39;re all within 3 1/2 mile radius I heard.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3706-->
<!--Post: 3819--><!--Time: 1105295252-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3819"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 09, 2005 - 10:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Q: <BR> <BR>No talk of BTK being out and about any more than usual. Just speculation over whether or not he would be trolling the net if using a public computer at library, lol. Poor guy must be having withdrawls by now. We were without power for a night and about half of a day. That was enough for me. It&#39;s damned cold here.  <BR> <BR>Evergreen Park is very close to North Riverside. All confirmed murders in 3 1/2 mile radius. Wichita is a small town. You can&#39;t hardly go from east side to west side without passing a crime scene or drop location.  <BR> <BR>Have you or has anyone you know contacted UNSUB Productions? I considered it and then digressed - the last time I tried to get with film makers &#40;UK&#41; Mr. Cougar had a meltdown over it. It&#39;s bad enough I&#39;m on the net and out taking pics. He didn&#39;t want me to become so involved. I guess I don&#39;t blame him. However, it is in my plan today to get out and photograph the Kechi and Kansas street locations.  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3819-->
<!--Post: 3842--><!--Time: 1105318663-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3842"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 09, 2005 - 4:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->401 North Kansas Street <BR>[IMG]<a href="http://img26.exs.cx/img26/8717/401northkansasstreet9zo.jpg" target=_top>http://img26.exs.cx/img26/8717/401northkansasstree t9zo.jpg</a>[/IMG] <BR> <BR>Looking North from 401 North Kansas Street you can see I-35 overpass.  <BR>[IMG]<a href="http://img26.exs.cx/img26/4384/northkansasstreet3is.jpg" target=_top>http://img26.exs.cx/img26/4384/northkansasstreet3i s.jpg</a>[/IMG] <BR> <BR>A little further up the block. I-35 to the right. <BR>[IMG]<a href="http://img26.exs.cx/img26/7955/northkansaslookingnoethati351x.jpg" target=_top>http://img26.exs.cx/img26/7955/northkansaslookingn oethati351x.jpg</a>[/IMG] <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3842-->
