<!--Post: 3854--><!--Time: 1105329968-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3854"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 09, 2005 - 8:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->You really knocked on the door? <BR> <BR>Maybe Mr. Cougar is right... I hope he was with you. <BR> <BR>Check the plastic porch chair... maybe someone sits out there and eats some day old BK from time to time... jk... maybe... <BR> <BR>I like your moxie! <BR> <BR>One other place I&#39;d like you to check if your out sluething... Dr. Moulds office around the corner from the Otero home... I think it&#39;s on Central. My question is how tall is the building and could someone inside see the Otero home from any of the windows or roof top?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3854-->
<!--Post: 3858--><!--Time: 1105333581-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3858"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 09, 2005 - 9:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There are no tall buildings anywhere near and of the crime scenes, no way to see into the Otero house unless you drove by one of the streets.  Plus, if this fellow you named and I won&#39;t, probably did not have an office 31 years ago.  Unless he is at least 55 now he was still in college in 1974.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3858-->
<!--Post: 3860--><!--Time: 1105335319-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3860"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 09, 2005 - 9:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->He... is older than 55 I believe. <BR> <BR>Also moving there after 1974 doesn&#39;t make it any less weird of a circumstance... in perspective. <BR> <BR>Let me just state that &#40;I know this is off topic&#41; I&#39;m not suggesting &#34;he&#34; is guilty of anything... <BR>BTK surely knows the area and might know the office building on perhaps a professinal basis as in patiant??? <BR> <BR>Your point about &#34;no tall buildings&#34; is noted but as such one at a angle with minimal height could perhaps... see the home???<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3860-->
<!--Post: 3877--><!--Time: 1105374995-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3877"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Analyzer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Analyzer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 10, 2005 - 8:36 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Q <BR> <BR>Here is the info on 5120 E. Central <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.sedgwickcounty.org/realpropertyinfo/RPDetail.cfm?ControlNum=155590" target=_top>http://www.sedgwickcounty.org/realpropertyinfo/RPD etail.cfm?ControlNum=155590</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3877-->
<!--Post: 3884--><!--Time: 1105383157-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3884"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 10, 2005 - 10:52 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->No, Q. I didn&#39;t knock on the door. I may be insane but I&#39;m not crazy, lol. It just looked deserted. No cars or lights. Probably no power. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3884-->
<!--Post: 3888--><!--Time: 1105393986-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3888"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 10, 2005 - 1:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->4 Stories Hmmmm... tall enough to see over the short distance to 803 N. Edgemoor???<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3888-->
<!--Post: 4401--><!--Time: 1106321946-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4401"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 7:39 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Q: <BR> <BR>As you drive south on Edgemoor from the Otero home, the road falls gently toward Central.  By the time you reach Central you have dropped about 8 to 10 feet. There is a Kansas National Guard Armory on the east side of Edgemoor about two blocks south of the Otero home.  Portions of it are tall enough to watch the Otero home, and the angle is good for watching the garage door &#40;which faces south, the front door faces east&#41; <BR> <BR>The building at 5120 E CENTRAL is an old light gray brick office building.  It is one story high, one office deep, and four offices wide.  The Otero home is not visible from any part of it. <BR> <BR><a href="mailto:Whoisbtk@yahoo.com">Whoisbtk@yahoo.com</a> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4401-->
<!--Post: 4900--><!--Time: 1106799973-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4900"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 8:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey Cougar and Whois: <BR> <BR>Note: The box was found on a road &#34;North of Ketchi&#34; <BR> <BR>Tom said he got a email a day before the drop from a women in a QT that saw a man open his wallet and he had a picture of Nancy Fox in it... he was asking directions if i recall Tom&#39;s message correctly. <BR> <BR>This QT is North of Ketchi... in fact it is &#34;on&#34; the North East corner of road called &#34;Ketchi&#34; I believe. <BR> <BR>A person in the chat yesterday called &#34;dreamer&#34; posted links to some maps. <BR> <BR>The first had a green line coming from the north &#40;off map&#41; south/right turn to a stop at... get this... Carol Moulds House. <BR> <BR>The road Carol Mould lived on is rt something but... becomes &#34;Ketchi&#34; something or other. <BR> <BR>I was told the names of some of these were changed such as 61st... <BR> <BR>When I asked said person &#40;dreamer&#41; why they had posted the map to Moulds Home... All I got was &#34;Who knows Q&#34; and &#34;I was just throwing it out there...trying to help&#34; <BR> <BR>Then &#34;dreamer&#34; quit chat... <BR> <BR>Hmmm... <BR> <BR>Tom told me he does not know who this is... <BR> <BR>Of course I have been in the chat before and saw some slightly sarcastic refs to Glen Campbell Lyrics &#40;actually song titles&#41; and assumed they were directed at me but would the bored and or intoxicated go this far to poke fun at me... doubt it! <BR> <BR>Really strange... especially when you keep in mind the only reason &#34;North of Ketchi&#34; came up was a apparent &#40;still not sure&#41; Map Quest snafu with the local of &#34;B&amp;K Storage&#34; at 11th &amp; Woodrow but listed as just &#34;North of Ketchi&#34; with no #s. <BR> <BR>That Dennis guy said he was in the general 11th &amp; Woodrow area &#40;my deduction by his description&#41; and got a strange feeling when he was there. <BR> <BR>Odd... Odd... Odd... <BR> <BR>Also: Post Toasties Corn Flakes in the past gave away: <BR> <BR>Train Sets <BR> <BR>Badges <BR> <BR>A Linda &#34;Williams&#34; Doll <BR> <BR>And a puppet set that has a display with cartoon children manipulating the puppets with strings that look like blind cords that go out a window &#40;see photos&#41;. <BR> <BR>Interested in your thoughts Cougar and Whois... also Analyzer if your reading this. <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR>Here are the cereal box photo links: <BR> <BR><a href="http://theimaginaryworld.com/box60.jpg" target=_top>http://theimaginaryworld.com/box60.jpg</a> <BR><a href="http://theimaginaryworld.com/box61.jpg" target=_top>http://theimaginaryworld.com/box61.jpg</a> <BR> <BR> <BR><a href="http://theimaginaryworld.com/rnn28.jpg" target=_top>http://theimaginaryworld.com/rnn28.jpg</a> <BR><a href="http://theimaginaryworld.com/rnn29.jpg" target=_top>http://theimaginaryworld.com/rnn29.jpg</a> <BR> <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.timepassagesnostalgia.com/watermarked/images05/0553gmanad1.jpg" target=_top>http://www.timepassagesnostalgia.com/watermarked/i mages05/0553gmanad1.jpg</a> <BR> <BR> <BR><a href="http://theimaginaryworld.com/tic395.jpg" target=_top>http://theimaginaryworld.com/tic395.jpg</a> <BR> <BR> <BR>Side Note: The drop site was near the: <BR>Atchison Topeka &amp; Santa Fe RR <BR> <BR>Also a song covered by many including the oft associated with &#34;Kansas&#34; Judy Garland. <BR> Interesting too... there are a lot of &#34;versions&#34; of the lyrics. <BR> <BR>Lyrics: <a href="http://www.google.com/search?hl=en&amp;lr=&amp;q=Atchison%2BTopeka%2BSanta%2BFe%2Blyrics&amp;btnG=Search" target=_top>http://www.google.com/search?hl=en&amp;lr=&amp;q=Atchison&#43; Topeka&#43;Santa&#43;Fe&#43;lyrics&amp;btnG=Search</a> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4900-->
<!--Post: 4903--><!--Time: 1106800626-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4903"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Analyzer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Analyzer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 8:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Q <BR> <BR>It is probably a copy of a map that I have posted here and on a few other sites as well.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4903-->
<!--Post: 4912--><!--Time: 1106812975-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4912"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 12:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Are you &#34;dreamer&#34; A? <BR> <BR>And why the lone Carol Mould Map?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4912-->
<!--Post: 4933--><!--Time: 1106832205-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4933"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 27, 2005 - 5:23 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Q, I wondered when this topic would pick up again. I have had nothing new to add to it, even with the latest drop, other than that I noticed imediately that the location was between Valley Center and Park City, west and a little north maybe of Kechi. I&#39;ve been waiting for you, buddy.  <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t know what to make of it yet. The other day when KAKE had yet to disclose the new drop&#39;s location jyn and I wagered bets on which direction from Wichita it would be. She said south. And on a hunch &#40; based on this topic right here &#41;I said north. BOOYAH!  <BR> <BR>I am going to take some time with the maps this morning. To think that just a couple of weeks ago I was up this way, driving with my two year old, looking for anything remarkable about the area, gives me the willies. Twice I went. Once I turned around and went home because I had the weirdest feeling that something was wrong.  <BR> <BR>What do you make of it all? Is there a connection? And where do we go from here? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
