<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5712"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:williammichael@direcway.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 01, 2005 - 3:05 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The &#34;machine gun&#34; is likely an automatic &#39;assault rifle&#39; type, which almost all police forces have something similar.  IF it seems silly for Kechi to have it, near me is the small town of Caddo, about the same size as Kechi.  In 1978 there was a shootout between escaped convicts and 4 LE officers, leaving 3 State Patrolment dead &#40;as well as several convicts&#41;.   Hopefully, Chief Moreland will need his machine gun, but who knows? <BR> <!--/Text--></td></tr>
