<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6071"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 5:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Kechi and Rail Roads <BR> <BR> “A Cyclopedia Of State History”, written by Frank W. Blackmar, was published in 1912.  &#40;The information was collected in 1910.&#41;  It describes Kechi as a village on the Chicago, Rock Island &amp; Pacific R. R., with a population of 100, located 8 miles northeast of Wichita.  &#40;<a href="http://skyways.lib.ks.us/genweb/archives/1912/k/kechi.html" target=_top>http://skyways.lib.ks.us/genweb/archives/1912/k/ke chi.html</a>&#41; <BR> <BR>CRI&amp;P was declared bankrupt in the early 1980s. An excellent online history of the railroad can be found at the Rock Island Technical Society website: <a href="http://www.simpson.edu/~RITS/" target=_top>http://www.simpson.edu/~RITS/</a>. <BR> <BR>Kechi is listed in an article on historic railroad depots, <a href="http://www.simpson.edu/~RITS/structures/ckndepotsmatrow/cknmatrow.html" target=_top>http://www.simpson.edu/~RITS/structures/ckndepotsm atrow/cknmatrow.html</a>, which shows a depot built by CK&amp;N railroad for the CRI&amp;P in Kechi, Kansas.  The article notes that the depots, often the largest buildings in the towns, were used for dances, church services, schools, and other social gatherings.  The depots were 22ft wide and 45-55 ft long. [Link to Kechi depot photo circa 1905: <a href="http://kechiks.com/historickechi/kechipic06.html" target=_top>http://kechiks.com/historickechi/kechipic06.html</a>] <BR> <BR> <BR><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com">whoisbtk@yahoo.com</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6071-->
<!--Post: 7458--><!--Time: 1108505813-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7458"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Analyzer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Analyzer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 2:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I can&#39;t take credit for this as I built it based upon a posting by Christen Iman on another site of interest.  <BR>I found that analysis highly interesting. <BR> <BR><a href="http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v622/JMTTS/Wichita18.jpg" target=_top>http://img.photobucket.com/albums/v622/JMTTS/Wichi ta18.jpg</a> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7458-->
<!--Post: 7472--><!--Time: 1108511679-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7472"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Featherw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Featherw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 3:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://www.ksdot.org/burtransplan/maps/city-pdf/ke" target=_top>http://www.ksdot.org/burtransplan/maps/city-pdf/ke</a> chi.pdf  <BR> <BR>City of Kechi...Sedgewick County..Kansas <BR>============== <BR>Here is an excellent map of Kechi...shows railroad tracks by symbol...thanks...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7472-->
<!--Post: 7482--><!--Time: 1108515324-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7482"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 4:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My family has an abstract on their home, and just out of curiosity one day I reviewed it. Of course it was several inches thick, and indeed the railroad was a large part of Park City/Kechi in the early 1900&#39;s. The area was quite large and it ran from Broadway E through Kechi &#40;the tracks are still there&#41;on 61st. Then North to Newton. I also have family in Newton, and the railroad was a very large part of the economy in the early 1900&#39;s.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7482-->
<!--Post: 7484--><!--Time: 1108515705-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7484"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 5:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The Qtrip you all are inquiring about above, is on the corner of 61st and Jacksonville. Just E. of I-135. Why are you looking for the Qtrip?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7484-->
<!--Post: 7499--><!--Time: 1108522446-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7499"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 6:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->a quck note: <BR> <BR>I&#39;m not sure where the &#34;north of Kechi&#34; reference came from...but, could whoever said it have meant north of kiowa, which would put it at the proper streets and fits in with a &#34;Keeper of the Plains&#34; reference I&#39;m looking at.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7499-->
<!--Post: 7500--><!--Time: 1108524469-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7500"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 7:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->also: <BR> <BR>which direction does it face? ewns<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7500-->
<!--Post: 7583--><!--Time: 1108587807-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7583"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 1:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky Wrote: Why are you looking for the Qtrip? <BR> <BR>Answer: We weren&#39;t looking for it per say Rocky. I wanted to know if it is on the &#34;North&#34; side of 61st &#40;kechi&#41; N.East corner or N.W. corner. <BR> <BR>A woman in this QT saw a man with a picture of Nancy Fox in his wallet, a day or so before the last drop in the area. <BR> <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42; <BR> <BR>Bmodule Wrote: &#34;I&#39;m not sure where the &#34;north of Kechi&#34; reference came from...&#34; <BR> <BR> <BR>It is layed out thru out the thread Bmodule but the basic starting point can be found in post #5 of this thread.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7583-->
<!--Post: 7622--><!--Time: 1108608939-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7622"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 6:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Q - the Quiktrip is on the northwest corner of 61st and Jacksonville. The Cracker Barrel is across the street. It wouldn&#39;t be hard to make it over to that Quiktrip from that last drop. Seneca to 61st street! Wow,is she sure it was Ms.Fox? By the way the picture that Melissa posted on AMW does look familiar!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7622-->
<!--Post: 7751--><!--Time: 1108672312-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7751"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 12:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rocky this incident at QT was a day or so &#34;before&#34; the drop. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7751-->
<!--Post: 7778--><!--Time: 1108680135-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7778"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bakerwood<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bakerwood<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 2:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bmodule, <BR>The Keeper of the plains faces roughly south.  I don&#39;t remember when the great statue was completed but I am curious about your reference to it.  Where would be an appropriate topic for your ideas?  <BR>And as a means of keeping on topic...the Kechi people were a clan of the Kiowa,&#40;A.K.A. Kaw, Kansa&#41; Indians all of which were names used to refer to the folks for whom the state was named. <BR> <BR>I&#39;m not smart, I just happen to have stopped at a museum last week that had a smart curator. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7778-->
<!--Post: 8295--><!--Time: 1109040669-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8295"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 6:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Q -  This was seen before the drop? My list of freaks just got a lot longer.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8295-->
<!--Post: 8297--><!--Time: 1109041483-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8297"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 7:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bmodule, isn&#39;t the Keeper of the Plains the tall indian statue by the Wichita Indian Museum over by cowtown? Sims &amp; Riverside I think. If so, it faces the West!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8297-->
<!--Post: 8320--><!--Time: 1109053098-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8320"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 10:18 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks. <BR> <BR>My original thought was that it was facing west. <BR> <BR>The reason I asked is that BTK seems to plant clues to misdirect the search rather than worry about the clues that he might leave.  <BR> <BR>Take for instance the mention from &#34;The Alleged BTK&#34; in the &#34;MESSAGES FROM BTK&#34; thread: <BR> <BR>&#34;I whooped like an indian walking down Arrowhead, turning left on Iroquois.&#34; <BR> <BR>The only way he could turn left on Iroquois from Arrowhead would be if he was walking away from 13th and going toward  Mc Lean Boulivard.  <BR> <BR>Why would he walk down a residential street attracting attention to himself and end up on a busy boulivard when he could park his car along 13th Street &#40;Indian Hill Shopping Center&#41; and drive away. <BR> <BR>The &#34;Keeper of the Plains&#34; came to mind from &#34;Chief&#34; and &#34;rooster&#34;, and when I was thinking that it faced west, I started looking east. Sorry I didn&#39;t clarify earlier but I forgot which string I was on and became distracted before I got around to running a search. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8320-->
</table></td></tr></table>
